# Llama 3.2 3B Instruct (meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct: 3.2B dense; Llama 3.2 Community License,
# gated repo; the HF token must have accepted it), official bf16 checkpoint (the original/ Meta
# copy in the repo is not downloaded): the Meta point of the speed/quality study
# (reports/speed_quality/). No thinking mode. The template always injects a system header
# ("Cutting Knowledge Date: December 2023", "Today Date: <today>"), so the rendered prompt carries
# the day's date. --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 and --max-num-seqs=16 as in the other presets;
# --generation-config=vllm ignores the upload's sampling defaults; 0.90 of the GPU.
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL_REVISION=0cb88a4f764b7a12671c53f0838cd831a0843b95
JEVEMU_VLLM_DTYPE=bfloat16
JEVEMU_VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
JEVEMU_VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.90
JEVEMU_VLLM_DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS=
JEVEMU_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS='--max-num-seqs=16 --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 --generation-config=vllm'
